WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.150 --> 00:00:03.950
So fuel the same careful way, every single time.

2
00:00:04.200 --> 00:00:06.025
Here’s the routine.

3
00:00:06.275 --> 00:00:10.900
Moor the boat securely, and if it’s practical, put your passengers ashore.

4
00:00:11.150 --> 00:00:14.400
Stop the engines and every electric motor.

5
00:00:14.650 --> 00:00:17.275
No smoking, no open flame.

6
00:00:17.525 --> 00:00:20.575
Close the hatches, ports and cabin doors.

7
00:00:20.825 --> 00:00:22.475
Why close up?

8
00:00:23.475 --> 00:00:27.925
Because the vapor is heavier than air, and you don’t want it flowing below.

9
00:00:28.175 --> 00:00:33.425
Keep the nozzle touching the fill pipe the whole time, which prevents a static spark.

10
00:00:33.675 --> 00:00:35.725
And don’t fill to the brim.

11
00:00:35.975 --> 00:00:38.300
Fuel expands as it warms.

12
00:00:38.550 --> 00:00:48.675
When you’re done, wipe up any spills, open everything back up, run the blower for at least four minutes, and sniff the bilge and the engine space before you turn the key.

13
00:00:48.925 --> 00:00:50.725
Close up to fuel.

14
00:00:50.975 --> 00:00:52.850
Open up to start.
